HeyContent Waitlist Overview
Objective:
Create a buzzworthy, shareable waitlist experience for HeyContent that builds anticipation, encourages referrals, and rewards early adopters with a personalized Creator Identity Card.

🛠️ What We’re Building
1. A Smart, Social Waitlist System

Users sign up with their email and answer 3–5 fun, branded onboarding questions (e.g., their content type, vibe, goals).

They’re then placed in a queue and told they’ll be emailed once it’s their turn.

They can wait or move up the line by inviting others or sharing their card.

2. A Personalized Creator Identity Card

Once signed up (and optionally queued), users receive a digital card they can save and share.

The card includes:

Their first name or creator name

A fun, AI-generated title (e.g., “Momentum Builder,” “Creative Alchemist”)

A branded HeyContent logo instead of the Arc leaf

A “Join Date” stamp for that collectible feel

A unique invite code or share link (with tracking)

Optional card variant if they invite friends

3. Viral Growth Incentive

Each user gets 3 invites to give away.

Referring others can bump their place in the line or unlock special editions of their card (like animated backgrounds, gold borders, etc.).

We reward early participation and sharing, not just speed.

🧠 Creative & Technical Notes
Design should feel clean, playful, and creator-focused (think Arc meets Spotify Wrapped with a sprinkle of Duolingo energy).

The HeyContent logo replaces the Arc icon and anchors the visual identity.

We should be able to generate cards dynamically with user data (e.g., name, title, join date, referral code).

Share actions (Twitter, Instagram Story, LinkedIn, etc.) should be optimized with OG tags for previews.

Email delivery (e.g., via Resend or SendGrid) will send them their card once they join or reach the front.